# Data layer

Contracts and status per microservice: `docs/07-integrations.md`. Types: `docs/05-data-models.md`.

## Clients

- One shared HTTP client factory (base URL, auth, interceptors, error normalization). Every microservice client
  is created from it. Never call `fetch`/axios ad hoc from a route or component.
- Today the client and `formatApiResponseError` are duplicated (`private-panel/api/http.ts`,
  `public-panel/api/http.ts`, `notifications/api/errors.ts`, …). Consolidation into one module (target:
  `libs/api-client`) is a tracked task. New code must not add another copy: import an existing one and note the
  duplication, or ask.
- Base URLs come only from env vars documented in `docs/08-configuration.md`. Browser calls go through the
  same-origin `/api` rewrite or proxy unless a doc says otherwise; never hardcode hosts.
- Errors are normalized into one typed shape (status, code, Persian message, field errors). UI maps them to
  states; it never parses raw backend errors itself.
- When an OpenAPI spec exists for a service, types are generated from it; do not hand-write DTOs that the spec
  covers. Until then, hand-written DTOs live in the service `types` module and are marked provisional.

## Server state

- Server state lives in the query cache, not in component state or global stores. Query keys come from one
  factory per service (`<service>Keys.list(filters)`, `<service>Keys.detail(id)`).
- Explicit `staleTime` per data type: long for categories, reasons, static pages (terms/help); short for
  messages, notifications, wallet balance, voucher/receipt state.
- After a mutation, invalidate exactly the affected keys. No blanket invalidation.
- No optimistic updates for payments, wallet, registrations, approvals, deletes or anything with money or
  moderation consequences. Optimistic UI is allowed only for low-risk toggles (pin, favourite, archive in Msg).

## Lists

- Panel lists (admin/provider/user panels): server-side pagination, 24 records per page unless the SRS path says
  otherwise. Public lists that the SRS marks as infinite scroll use cursor/page infinite queries.
- Filter, sort, search and page live in the URL query string so views are shareable and back-button safe.
- Debounce search/filter inputs by at least 300 ms. Enforce SRS input limits (search ≤ 50 characters).
- Never fetch-all-then-slice on the client. Exception: a `mock/` implementation may filter/sort in memory to
  simulate the server, as long as the UI calls `api/` with the same params it will send to the real endpoint.

## Mocks

- Mock data has the exact shape of the real contract, including pagination meta and error shape.
- Mock `api/` implementations simulate latency and the SRS exception paths (duplicate name, in-use delete,
  upload format/size, guest access) so every E-path has a reachable UI.
